        </ezobject:attribute>
        <ezobject:attribute xmlns:ezremote="http://ez.no/ezobject" ezremote:id="720" ezremote:identifier="intro" name="Summary" type="ezxmltext">
          <section xmlns:image="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/image/" xmlns:xhtml="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/xhtml/" xmlns:custom="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/custom/"><paragraph>This tutorial shows developers how one Exponential installation serves any number of websites. You learn how siteaccesses work and apply them to build two multilingual websites on a single Exponential instance.</paragraph></section>
        </ezobject:attribute>
        <ezobject:attribute xmlns:ezremote="http://ez.no/ezobject" xmlns:xhtml="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/xhtml/" ezremote:id="721" ezremote:identifier="body" name="Body" type="ezxmltext">
          <section xmlns:image="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/image/" xmlns:xhtml="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/xhtml/" xmlns:custom="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/custom/"><section><header>Introduction</header><paragraph>Users of Exponential sometimes wonder whether one installation can serve several websites. It can, through the siteaccess. Siteaccesses do much more than host several sites in one installation. With them you can:</paragraph><paragraph><ul><li><paragraph>share content, classes and users between sites</paragraph></li><li><paragraph>show the same content in several places with additional locations</paragraph></li><li><paragraph>give each site its own design, languages and settings while keeping one code base</paragraph></li><li><paragraph>upgrade every site at once, because they share one installation</paragraph></li></ul></paragraph><paragraph>The full guide is part of the <link href="https://doc.exponential.earth">Exponential documentation</link>.</paragraph></section><section><header>About this tutorial</header><paragraph>This tutorial is maintained by 7x for the Exponential Foundation and updated for Exponential 6.0.15.</paragraph></section></section>
